242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 18 0 R
/E (Our older robots used mercury-tilt switches that were nothing more than on-off contacts. They chattered on every bump, needed separate sensors for nose-up and nose-down. By replacing them with a single BNO080 IMU we now read yaw, pitch, and roll angles, giving us more information.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [223]
>>
endobj
